<article class="env-lemma" id="0DN7">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DN7">Lemma <span data-tag="0DN7">101.33.4</span>.</a> Let $f : \mathcal{X} \to \mathcal{Y}$ be a morphism of algebraic stacks. Let $\mathcal{Z} \to \mathcal{Y}$ be a surjective, flat, locally finitely presented morphism of algebraic stacks. If the base change $\mathcal{Z} \times _\mathcal {Y} \mathcal{X} \to \mathcal{Z}$ is smooth, then $f$ is smooth. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The property “smooth” satisfies the conditions of Lemma <a href="/tag/0DN6" data-tag="0DN6">101.27.10</a>. Smooth local on the source-and-target we have seen in the introduction to this section and fppf local on the target is Descent on Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/0429" data-tag="0429">74.11.26</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>